  body: "# Beneficial and legal capital ownership in JSA(IB) and IS\n\n## Authored interpretation\n\n\
    The captured capital chapter distinguishes a beneficial interest from holding capital in one’s name
    and explains that a legal owner may hold capital on trust for another beneficial owner.\n\n## Scope
    and exceptions\n\nAn account name alone does not resolve beneficial ownership. Joint interests, trusts,
    evidence presumptions and particular assets need separate examination. Chapter 29 says capital does
    not affect JSA(Cont); no capital rule is transferred to Pension Credit or another benefit. This is
    an unreviewed research concept, not a property-law determination.\n\n## Inspected source passages\n\
    \n- [DMG 29070, PDF page 9](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/69d8f3a496c86b751317022c/dmg-Ch-29.pdf#page=9)
    — DMG Vol 5 Ch 29: Capital.\n- [DMG 29071, PDF page 9](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/69d8f3a496c86b751317022c/dmg-Ch-29.pdf#page=9)
    — DMG Vol 5 Ch 29: Capital.\n- [DMG 29072, PDF page 9](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/69d8f3a496c86b751317022c/dmg-Ch-29.pdf#page=9)
    — DMG Vol 5 Ch 29: Capital.\n- [DMG 29074, PDF page 9](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/69d8f3a496c86b751317022c/dmg-Ch-29.pdf#page=9)
    — DMG Vol 5 Ch 29: Capital.\n- [DMG 29000, PDF page 3](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/69d8f3a496c86b751317022c/dmg-Ch-29.pdf#page=3)
    — DMG Vol 5 Ch 29: Capital.\n\n## Evidence and review status\n\nModel-assisted interpretation of selected
    passages in the 15 September 2026 frozen source snapshot. Specialist review is required. Source acquisition,
    source revision, legal effective dates and this record’s authoring time are separate.\n\nThis is an
    independent experimental publication, not an official DWP document, individual advice, an entitlement
    decision or an executable rule. Machine-extracted text may alter reading order, footnotes and characters.
    No PDF visual inspection, whole-chapter coverage or behavioural evaluation pass is claimed by this
    record.\n\n- `dmg-vol5-ch29`: PDF SHA-256 `a1b086fdad8d32d6273b35fb8895516b6957faacd05fd3b06e091032598a47b9`;
    extracted pages SHA-256 `b490507e3aaf6110ea0593fee2ee4d772fd5a1f9a75f4f91008734caec51cfd9`.\n"
  semantic_relations:
  - target: term/jsais-capital-deprivation
    predicate: http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related
    rationale: The deprivation provision expressly requires prior beneficial or joint beneficial
      ownership and distinguishes the claimant’s share from another person’s share.
    evidence:
    - page: page/dmg-vol5-ch29/0159
      quote: "29809 The law applies to claimants and partners only if they were the beneficial owner or
        joint beneficial\nowners of the capital. So if a claimant is the joint beneficial owner of a building
        society account which has\n£10,000 in it and the claimant's share is £4,000 the law\n\n\n1. applies
        if the claimant spends or gives away that £4,000 or any part of it for the purpose of getting\n\
        benefit or more benefit and\n\n\n2. does not apply if the other £6,000 or any part of it is spent
        or given away."
      locator: DMG 29809
